messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/gregbook/rpng-win.c
Line: 260
Function: WinMain
Bug type: stack-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-121
Explanation: The argv-building loop writes pointers into args[1024] without bounds checking (argv[argc++] = q = p;). A long command line with many space-separated tokens can make argc exceed 1023, causing writes past the end of the fixed-size stack array. The terminating write argv[argc] = NULL at line 269 can also overflow for the same reason, leading to stack memory corruption.

Source context:
```c
      220:             LUT_exponent = 1.0 / sgi_gamma;
      221:     }
      222: #elif defined(Macintosh)
      223:     LUT_exponent = 1.8 / 2.61;
      224:     /*
      225:     if (some_mac_function_that_returns_gamma(&mac_gamma))
      226:         LUT_exponent = mac_gamma / 2.61;
      227:      */
      228: #else
      229:     LUT_exponent = 1.0;   /* assume no LUT:  most PCs */
      230: #endif
      231: 
      232:     /* the defaults above give 1.0, 1.3, 1.5 and 2.2, respectively: */
      233:     default_display_exponent = LUT_exponent * CRT_exponent;
